    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d79">

                <pb facs="0170" n="50" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg50"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/3034</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Guggenheim</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-08">April 8, 1931</date>.<lb/>[Received April
                        10.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 637</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my despatch No. 618 of March
                    31, 1931,<anchor n="16" xml:id="d79-f1"/> I have the honor to report that the
                    Military Court has exonerated Major Espinosa, President Machado’s former Aide de
                    Camp, of all responsibility in connection with the placing of a bomb in the
                    palace on February 23. The soldier Camilo Valdés, who admitted placing the bomb
                    and whose confession implicated Espinosa and led to the latter’s indictment, has
                    been condemned to death, but it is believed that his sentence will be commuted
                    to life imprisonment.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry F.
                    Guggenheim</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
